                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jayanth Othayoth",
                        "email": "ojayanth@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ojayanth"
                    },
                    "message": "Please refer https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-certificate-manager/+/13364 patchset 9 comment related to this . Mutiple time we discussed this and rejected this check due to valid  concern related to RTC ."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Chandra Harkude",
                        "email": "Chandramohan.harkude@gmail.com",
                        "username": "chandramohan83"
                    },
                    "message": "My commit addresses the RTC concern properly. enforces expiration on install/replace but explicitly skips it at startup \u2014 which aligns with exactly what was agreed here: reject truly expired certs at install time, but don't block startup due to clock race conditions. That's\n  the right approach per this prior consensus"
                }
            ],
